00:29:14.850 --> 00:29:17.050
You know, they were doing the whip cuts.
你知道的，他们在做快速摇镜头。

662
00:29:17.250 --> 00:29:17.450
Right.
没错。

663
00:29:17.610 --> 00:29:18.650
To make it look frantic.
为了营造出慌乱感。

664
00:29:18.650 --> 00:29:19.130
Right.
对。

665
00:29:19.490 --> 00:29:26.550
Now, next up, lady, I thought we should discuss this moment that no one wrote in about, but
接下来，女士，我觉得我们应该讨论这个谁也没有发信来问，但

666
00:29:26.550 --> 00:29:27.610
that was so epic.
却极其精彩的瞬间。

667
00:29:27.950 --> 00:29:29.630
I can't believe no one wrote in about it.
我真不敢相信居然没人写信来问这事。

668
00:29:29.750 --> 00:29:33.950
I know exactly the moment you're talking about because it was such a big deal to all of us
我完全知道你在说哪个瞬间，因为这对我们所有片场的人

669
00:29:33.950 --> 00:29:34.550
on set.
来说都是件大事。

670
00:29:34.550 --> 00:29:39.770
And maybe people don't realize that because of what a badass Chris Workman is.
也许大家没意识到这一点，是因为克里斯·沃克曼太强悍了。

671
00:29:40.070 --> 00:29:46.310
So, what we're talking about is the moment when, led by Kevin, the Dunder Mifflin employees
所以，我们要讨论的就是那个瞬间：在凯文的带领下，邓德米夫林的员工们

672
00:29:46.310 --> 00:29:52.310
are running through the kitchen and take down our camera operator, Randall Einhorn.
冲过厨房，把我们的摄像师兰德尔·埃因霍恩给撞倒了。

673
00:29:52.590 --> 00:29:54.830
Guys, this was a total mistake.
伙计们，这完全是个意外。

674
00:29:55.190 --> 00:29:55.670
Yeah.
是啊。

675
00:29:55.910 --> 00:29:58.630
We were like, oh my God, Randall's down.
当时我们都惊了，天哪，兰德尔倒了。

676
00:29:59.070 --> 00:30:00.370
But only for a few seconds.
但也就几秒钟的事。

677
00:30:00.590 --> 00:30:05.290
We reached out to Randall because we had to hear this story from his perspective.
我们联系了兰德尔，因为我们必须听听他视角里的这个故事。

678
00:30:05.470 --> 00:30:07.290
When Brian mowed him down.
当布莱恩把他撞倒的时候。

679
00:30:07.790 --> 00:30:13.150
I remember when I was running backwards through the break room and Brian Baumgartner, who plays
我记得当时我正倒着穿过休息室，扮演凯文的布莱恩·鲍姆加特纳

680
00:30:13.150 --> 00:30:16.510
Kevin, was running at me because he's frantically trying to get out of there.
正向我跑来，因为他拼命想逃离那里。

681
00:30:16.910 --> 00:30:21.690
And he just kept running on me, running and gaining on me and gaining on me.
他一直冲向我，越跑越近，越跑越近。

682
00:30:21.730 --> 00:30:23.150
And I'm running backwards with the camera.
而我正扛着摄像机倒着跑。

683
00:30:23.510 --> 00:30:25.890
And he just got so close that I think he hit me.
他靠得实在太近了，我想他撞到了我。

684
00:30:26.010 --> 00:30:27.430
And I hit the ground.
然后我摔倒了。

685
00:30:27.430 --> 00:30:28.230
I went down.
我倒地了。

686
00:30:28.510 --> 00:30:34.170
But my camera assist, Chris Workman, who's a really strong guy, just caught me with one
但我的摄像助理克里斯·沃克曼，一个非常强壮的家伙，只用了一只

687
00:30:34.170 --> 00:30:38.210
arm, caught me and the camera with one arm and put me back on my feet.
胳膊就拉住了我，单臂托住我和摄像机，把我重新扶了起来。

688
00:30:38.370 --> 00:30:40.410
And I'm like a 200-pound guy.
我可是一个两百磅的壮汉。

689
00:30:40.530 --> 00:30:42.170
The camera's nearly 40 pounds.
摄像机也将近四十磅重。

690
00:30:42.370 --> 00:30:43.870
And Chris just lifted me up.
而克里斯就这样把我提了起来。

691
00:30:43.910 --> 00:30:45.390
I didn't even know if I hit the ground.
我甚至都不知道自己有没有倒地。

692
00:30:46.410 --> 00:30:50.690
But that shot of me going down and getting back up actually made the show.
但那个我倒地又站起来的镜头最后确实剪进了正片里。

693
00:30:50.890 --> 00:30:52.890
So, thank you, Chris Workman, for picking me up.
所以，谢谢你，克里斯·沃克曼，把我拉了起来。

694
00:30:52.970 --> 00:30:56.390
And thank you, Brian Baumgartner, for running into me and making such a cool shot.
也谢谢你，布莱恩·鲍姆加特纳，撞倒了我并成就了这么酷的一个镜头。

695
00:30:58.530 --> 00:31:03.890
Well, Angela, I felt like we also needed to hear from Brian Baumgartner about this moment.
好吧，安吉拉，我觉得我们还得听听布莱恩·鲍姆加特纳对这个瞬间的看法。

696
00:31:04.170 --> 00:31:05.730
The mower and the mode.
撞人者与被撞者的视角。

697
00:31:06.090 --> 00:31:06.610
Exactly.
没错。

698
00:31:07.010 --> 00:31:08.670
We needed a point counterpoint.
我们需要针锋相对的观点。

699
00:31:09.410 --> 00:31:11.730
Well, thank you, Randall.
好吧，谢谢你，兰德尔。

700
00:31:12.070 --> 00:31:15.130
You know, I wanted to make fun of you for getting the story wrong.
你知道的，我本来想取笑你把故事记错了呢。

701
00:31:15.130 --> 00:31:19.130
But you complimented me and got the story 100% right.
但你夸了我，而且把故事完全百分之百说对了。

702
00:31:19.310 --> 00:31:22.670
I mean, look, I had people running behind me, okay?
我是说，听着，当时我身后有人在追，好吗？

703
00:31:22.670 --> 00:31:28.970
So, I had to run over whatever was in front of me or I would have gotten run over myself.
所以，我必须从挡在前面的任何东西上面踩过去，否则我自己就会被撞倒。

704
00:31:29.870 --> 00:31:36.750
But actually, come to think of it, it's the first time that anyone has ever told me that I've outrun anyone.
不过说实话，仔细想想，这还是头一次有人对我说我跑赢了别人。

705
00:31:37.030 --> 00:31:40.730
I mean, you were running backwards carrying a camera.
我的意思是，你当时可是倒着跑还扛着摄像机呢。

706
00:31:41.390 --> 00:31:44.590
But, yeah, I had to put you down.
不过，对，我不得不把你放倒。

707
00:31:44.590 --> 00:31:50.210
And, look, the thing I remember is, yes, you went all the way to your back, as I recall.
而且，你看，我记得最清楚的是，没错，据我回忆，你整个人是向后倒下去的。

708
00:31:50.390 --> 00:31:57.690
And for me, out of the corner of my eye, it looked like Chris Workman, one hand, picked you up, put you back on the feet.
对我来说，从眼角余光看过去，就像是克里斯·沃克曼单手把你扶起来，让你重新站稳。

709
00:31:57.830 --> 00:32:02.810
And like the pro that you are, well, you just kept filming.
而你就像个真正的专业人士一样，继续拍着。

710
00:32:03.050 --> 00:32:05.630
I'm so happy that it made it into the cut.
我很高兴这个镜头最终被剪辑进去了。

711
00:32:05.630 --> 00:32:07.590
And it's one of my favorite episodes.
而且这也是我最喜欢的剧集之一。

712
00:32:07.890 --> 00:32:09.810
It aired after the Super Bowl, obviously.
很显然，它是在超级碗之后播出的。

713
00:32:10.390 --> 00:32:12.670
And that was a big deal for me.
这对我来说可是件大事。

714
00:32:12.950 --> 00:32:16.310
And, yeah, one of our funniest cold opens, for sure.
而且，没错，绝对是我们最搞笑的开场戏之一。

715
00:32:16.750 --> 00:32:22.310
Well, lady, I just remember that moment so vividly because I do remember, Randall is down.
天哪，女士，我对那个时刻记忆犹新，因为我真的记得当时兰德尔倒下了。

716
00:32:22.310 --> 00:32:23.230
What do we do?
我们该怎么办？

717
00:32:23.410 --> 00:32:24.470
And then Randall is up.
然后兰德尔又站起来了。

718
00:32:24.590 --> 00:32:26.010
I guess we continue.
我想我们只能继续了。

719
00:32:26.470 --> 00:32:29.120
Amazing to me.
这让我觉得太神奇了。

720
00:32:29.320 --> 00:32:31.140
And that's the only time it happened.
而且那是唯一发生过的一次。

721
00:32:31.140 --> 00:32:32.780
And that's the take we used.
我们用的就是那个镜头。

722
00:32:33.180 --> 00:32:34.280
Chris Workman, man.
克里斯·沃克曼，天呐。

723
00:32:34.700 --> 00:32:36.080
He is a machine.
他简直就是个机器。

724
00:32:41.660 --> 00:32:42.500
PostMail about.
关于邮递员的。

725
00:32:42.780 --> 00:32:43.580
Oh, yeah?
哦，是吗？

726
00:32:45.060 --> 00:32:46.060
Save Bandits.
拯救班迪特。

727
00:32:49.250 --> 00:32:53.150
Now, Save Bandit was the last thing on our call sheet for the day.
现在，“拯救班迪特”是我们那天通告单上的最后一场戏。

728
00:32:53.390 --> 00:32:55.330
All the rest of us had gone home.
我们其余所有人都已经回家了。

729
00:32:55.510 --> 00:32:58.170
I know they did this because it was so complicated.
我知道他们这么安排是因为这太复杂了。

