00:32:58.190 --> 00:33:00.410
They wanted you to have the set to yourself.
他们想让你独自拥有整个片场。

731
00:33:00.730 --> 00:33:02.110
I was not there.
我当时不在场。

732
00:33:02.650 --> 00:33:06.990
Angela, please tell us, how did you pull this off?
安吉拉，请告诉我们，你是怎么做到的？

733
00:33:07.190 --> 00:33:09.410
Okay, so here's the thing, guys.
好吧，事情是这样的，各位。

734
00:33:09.470 --> 00:33:11.050
We had to have a lot of rehearsals.
我们必须进行大量的排练。

735
00:33:11.050 --> 00:33:15.210
You should know, on the day when there was a lot of the chaos and we were all running around,
你们应该知道，在那天充满混乱、我们都在到处跑的时候，

736
00:33:15.270 --> 00:33:20.070
I was there, but the cat didn't work those moments, okay?
我在场，但猫在那些时刻并没有出镜，好吗？

737
00:33:20.550 --> 00:33:20.930
Yeah.
对。

738
00:33:21.390 --> 00:33:27.170
The cat did have to work one moment, Jenna, with all of us, where I open the drawer and
珍娜，猫确实跟我们大家一起合作了一个镜头，就是我打开抽屉，然后

739
00:33:27.170 --> 00:33:27.790
you reveal.
你掀开。

740
00:33:28.130 --> 00:33:28.370
Yeah.
对。

741
00:33:28.370 --> 00:33:30.670
You guys are all in the background for that moment.
那个镜头你们大家都在背景里。

742
00:33:31.030 --> 00:33:36.610
And I had to actually pick the cat up and walk over to where I would have tossed it.
我实际上必须把猫抱起来，走到我要把它扔过去的地方。

743
00:33:36.750 --> 00:33:37.450
And that was it.
事情就是这样。

744
00:33:37.590 --> 00:33:40.350
That's all I had to do with the cat, with the group there.
这就是我在有大家在场的情况下，和这只猫有关的全部工作。

745
00:33:41.070 --> 00:33:42.410
Jenna, this cat was massive.
珍娜，这只猫太巨大了。

746
00:33:42.790 --> 00:33:43.890
It looks big.
它看起来确实很大。

747
00:33:44.050 --> 00:33:45.950
I'm like, did you cast the biggest cat they had?
我在想，你们是不是挑了他们能找到的最大的一只猫？

748
00:33:46.050 --> 00:33:48.730
Did you see the big one in the corner and say, we want that, dude?
你们是不是看到角落里那只大的就说，兄弟，我们就想要那只？

749
00:33:49.690 --> 00:33:55.110
Just taking it out of the drawer with the chaos, not even doing anything with it, just picking
仅仅是在混乱中把它从抽屉里拿出来，甚至都没对它做什么，只是把它抱起来

750
00:33:55.110 --> 00:33:59.710
it up and taking it to my spot, the cat was like, um, I'm out of here.
带到我的位置，那只猫的反应就像是，呃，我得撤了。

751
00:34:00.750 --> 00:34:06.510
So I was really glad when we actually filmed the stunt part that you guys were all gone.
所以我真的很高兴，当我们真正拍摄特技部分时，你们都已经不在了。

752
00:34:07.210 --> 00:34:07.610
Right.
对。

753
00:34:07.950 --> 00:34:08.850
Oh my gosh.
我的天哪。

754
00:34:09.010 --> 00:34:11.290
Less activity for the cat to deal with.
猫咪要应付的动静少多了。

755
00:34:11.390 --> 00:34:13.430
The cat was already like, where am I?
这只猫当时就已经觉得：我在哪儿？

756
00:34:13.490 --> 00:34:14.110
What's going on?
发生什么事了？

757
00:34:14.490 --> 00:34:14.930
All right.
好吧。

758
00:34:15.050 --> 00:34:16.950
So a lot of things went in to make this happen.
为了实现这个效果，有很多环节共同促成了它。

759
00:34:17.230 --> 00:34:21.110
And I'm going to share with you some stuff that Randy Cordray and Jeff Blitz shared with
接下来我要跟你们分享一些兰迪·科德雷和杰夫·布里茨告诉我

760
00:34:21.110 --> 00:34:21.250
me.
的事情。

761
00:34:21.370 --> 00:34:23.270
But then I'm going to tell you my personal memories.
不过随后我会告诉你们我个人的回忆。

762
00:34:23.770 --> 00:34:28.210
So I guess in the script, there were a few alts about how the cat got in the ceiling.
所以我猜在剧本里，关于猫是怎么钻进天花板，有几种不同的备选方案。

763
00:34:29.210 --> 00:34:34.030
Jeff Blitz fought really hard to have the moment where the cat goes up in the ceiling
杰夫·布里茨极力争取保留这样一个镜头：猫钻进了天花板，

764
00:34:34.030 --> 00:34:36.030
and then out a different part of the ceiling.
然后又从天花板的另一个地方钻出来。

765
00:34:36.270 --> 00:34:36.650
Yes.
没错。

766
00:34:36.810 --> 00:34:38.110
That was the thing he fought for.
那就是他极力争取的效果。

767
00:34:38.330 --> 00:34:44.690
He said to do this, though, it would involve a pair of matching cats and two trainers in
但他同时说过，要做到这一点，需要有一对长得一模一样的猫，以及两个训练师

768
00:34:44.690 --> 00:34:45.110
the ceiling.
在天花板上。

769
00:34:45.110 --> 00:34:52.370
One to catch bandit one and one to drop bandit two through a different ceiling panel.
一个用来接住“班迪一号”，另一个负责把“班迪二号”从不同的天花板嵌板处放下去。

770
00:34:52.770 --> 00:34:56.750
So the idea originally was that you would go on a search for twin cats.
所以最初的想法是，你们得去寻找双胞胎猫。

771
00:34:56.950 --> 00:34:57.510
Twin cats.
双胞胎猫。

772
00:34:57.510 --> 00:34:58.690
Identical looking cats.
外表完全一样的猫。

773
00:34:58.930 --> 00:34:59.190
Yes.
是的。

774
00:35:00.090 --> 00:35:05.690
And Randy said that we worked with an excellent animal training company out of Silmar, California.
兰迪说，我们当时跟加州西尔马的一家优秀动物驯养公司合作过。

775
00:35:06.030 --> 00:35:08.410
Their name is Bob Dunn's Animal Services.
他们的名字叫鲍勃·邓恩动物服务公司。

776
00:35:08.710 --> 00:35:14.110
And our specific cat trainer for this stunt and many more episodes was Denise Sanders.
而专门负责这场特技以及更多集数的猫咪驯养师是丹尼斯·桑德斯。

777
00:35:14.110 --> 00:35:15.370
She was fantastic.
她太棒了。

778
00:35:15.670 --> 00:35:16.630
I love Denise.
我超喜欢丹尼斯。

779
00:35:17.470 --> 00:35:21.550
And Randy would want you guys to know that we took the safety of not only the humans
兰迪想让你们知道，我们不仅对片场人类的安全非常重视，

780
00:35:21.550 --> 00:35:22.970
on set, but also the animals.
对动物也是如此。

781
00:35:23.110 --> 00:35:24.050
Took it very seriously.
我们对待安全问题非常严肃。

782
00:35:24.330 --> 00:35:25.370
Well, that was Randy.
好吧，这就是兰迪。

783
